{{Main|Australian federal election, 2010}}

This article provides a list of federal [[opinion polls]] that were conducted between the [[Australian federal election, 2007|2007 election]] and [[Australian federal election, 2010|2010 election]].

==Newspoll==
[[Newspoll]] federal polling consists of voting intention, better prime minister and leader satisfaction-dissatisfaction ratings, and is conducted via random telephone number selection in city and country areas nationwide, Friday to Sunday, usually each fortnight. [[Sample size|Sampling sizes]] consist of around 1100–1200 electors. The declared [[margin of error]] is ± 3 per cent.

